WEBVTT

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:06.060
Though it was only for the morning, going to school after all this time is tiring.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.900
From tomorrow on, we'll be attending the same school.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.900
Just how often have you mentioned that by now?

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.570
That's because... I'm happy about it.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.560
It couldn't be...

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.060
Riko...

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:46.370
I'm home, Onii-chan.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.180
tomodachi ni mo ienakatta

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.510
omoi wo tojikometa mama no

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:12.600
kokoro no naka mahou no furuutsu

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:17.570
tabereba tsutawaru... nante ne

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:23.180
kyoushitsu de matteita no, mada

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.180
guuzen da to iiwake shiteru

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.770
sono egao wa tabun dareka no mono

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:39.230
yume ga watashi no negai wo kanaeru nara

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:44.180
sotto agetai purezento yo

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.350
anata no niji shiawase ni todoku

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:54.310
hashi e to kaeru wa te wo futte ne

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:59.590
ii no ii no

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:04.940
mitsumeteitai dake nano...

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.780
<i>The Little Sister Who Returned</i>

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.880
It's been a while!

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.180
What's wrong? You're spacing out.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.290
Weirdo.

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:38.210
What about you, coming back all of a sudden without a word in advance?

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.210
Didn't you hear from Dad?

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.240
Not a thing.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:44.110
No way! Then you must've been surprised!

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.080
Yeah, I sure was!

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.730
Oh well! Come on in!

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:54.690
That's all right, I can carry it myself!

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.490
No need to hold back!

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.360
No, it's fine.

00:02:58.360 --> 00:02:59.720
Come on, let go!

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:00.990
I said it's fine!

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.110
You're as stubborn as ever when it comes to these things.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:06.910
Isn't it strange for you to be so attentive to your little sister?

00:03:07.430 --> 00:03:09.120
That's true as well...

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.330
It's good to be honest with yourself.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.170
Kirino-chan...

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:15.800
Riko-chan...

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.610
It's been a while.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.260
We're... together again.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:34.650
I'm back.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.570
Welcome home.

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:41.540
Anyway, let's go inside. No point standing around like this.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.660
You're right.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.670
Then I'll be going.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.870
Why?

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.830
I don't want to intrude on your longtime reunion.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.320
Kirino-chan...

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.720
See you tomorrow.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.340
Is she being considerate of me?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:57.590
It's okay, right?

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.050
Let's accept her gesture and have some sibling time together.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.540
I'm home!

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.040
Isn't it nice being able to come in saying that!

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.950
I'd be more concerned if you came in with a "Sorry to barge in!"

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:18.580
You still seem to be getting along well with Kirino.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:19.630
I guess.

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:20.550
I see.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.650
So, don't you ever clean in here?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:24.670
Once in a while.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.830
Is it really that dirty?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:31.870
If you can't even tell by yourself, I guess I'll just have to do it for you.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.250
Thanks.

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:34.430
We'll take shifts.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.700
Can I have some as well?

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.630
You're pretty dauntless to think nothing of an indirect kiss.

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:41.090
What are you talking about?

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:44.850
Delicious!

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:47.390
I'm going to put away my luggage.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.800
Can I leave them upstairs?

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.790
Your room hasn't changed.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:51.680
Thanks.

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:58.650
She's become pretty womanly.

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:02.150
She'll be a new family member from today on.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.170
This girl will be family?

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.950
H-Hello.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.270
I'm Fukamine...

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.200
Fukamine Riko.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:14.010
She's your age.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:17.000
But you said I would get a younger sister.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.570
It doesn't matter, right?

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.540
From today on it'll be us three.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.630
Please try to get along, you two.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:32.740
<i>She's cuter than Satou-san, the most popular girl in class!</i>

00:05:32.740 --> 00:05:33.780
<i>I'm shocked!</i>

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.210
P-Please take good care of me.

00:05:40.150 --> 00:05:41.440
Y-Yeah!

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:46.810
So she finally came back...

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:48.990
Onii-chan?

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.530
W-What!?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.410
I'm going to pick up my school uniform. Mind tagging along?

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:55.560
Ah, sure thing.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:58.320
What's wrong? Your face is red.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:05:59.810
N-Nothing.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.960
Let's go, baby!

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.960
<i>Narasaki Shopping District</i>

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:06.950
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.430
Does it suit me?

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.430
Why did you change already?

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:19.790
I thought I'd show you first thing.

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.660
What do you think?

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.440
D-Déjà vu.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:32.360
You know, this morning, Kirino came to wake me up in her school uniform as well.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.170
So you have Kirino wake you up in the morning.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:38.610
An alarm clock won't get me out of bed!

00:06:40.940 --> 00:06:42.070
I'm off to change.

00:06:42.070 --> 00:06:45.960
Hey, wait! It looks good! It looks great on you!

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.090
How convincing.

00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:49.810
I'm serious!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:54.400
It suits you. It looks cute.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:55.730
Thanks.

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.100
The atmosphere around here hasn't changed.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.870
Really?

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:09.150
You know that after my parents died, I've been living with relatives all over, right?

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.910
The first time you're in a new town is always a little scary.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.060
I'm glad it hasn't changed.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.750
If my father's business hadn't failed, you would've been able to stay here forever.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:28.780
I was able to come back again.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.720
I'm just happy for that right now.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.530
I'm truly grateful to have been called back here.

00:07:34.530 --> 00:07:36.430
You won't be sent off anywhere again.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:44.700
Amazing. There's real snow falling in this shop!

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.040
The Gift is still active in this town.

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:49.440
The rainbow's still up there too, right?

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.770
It's still there, huh?

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:57.750
They even established a research facility in the outskirts of town.

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:00.630
To investigate the eternal rainbow and Gift.

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:03.600
And guess who happens to work there!?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.020
Is something wrong?

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:07.920
It's nothing!

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:22.000
Damn, this is heavy!

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.080
Your refrigerator is empty anyway, isn't it?

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.300
You got that right...

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:28.100
Can't you carry some as well?

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:31.670
What? And you insisted on carrying my bag earlier.

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:32.780
Some gentleman you are.

00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.990
My courtesy expires quickly.

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:38.990
Be a little more appreciative of your little sister.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.490
"It's rough being a big brother," huh?

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:49.790
<i>My little sister, huh...</i>

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:56.470
That's all right, you don't need to do that.

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.470
But it's my job.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.660
Your job?

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.810
Who told you to do this?

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.480
I'm sorry!

00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:08.960
There you go apologizing at the drop of a hat again!

00:09:08.960 --> 00:09:10.320
I'm sorry!

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:16.320
We're family now.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:20.530
Isn't that right?

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:21.910
But...

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:26.140
Then how about this? From now on, you'll be my little sister.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:27.400
Your little sister?

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:30.960
So from now on you'll call me "Onii-chan."

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:32.530
O-Onii—

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:33.430
Onii-chan.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:36.840
Onii... chan.

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.710
Onii-chan.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.870
Great! I'll take over!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.890
Thanks, Onii-chan!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:52.920
Onii-chan?

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:54.900
What's up?

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:56.870
It's nothing!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.920
Man, I'm leaving you behind!

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.370
Something plain is fine for tonight!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.880
We have a welcoming party tomorrow anyway.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:14.900
You usually never eat properly in the first place, do you?

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.380
It's either take-out or warm-up meals in the evening.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.590
That's why men can't live on their own...

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:21.850
Then what about breakfast?

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:24.070
Kirino makes breakfast for me.

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.390
Are you even making her do that?

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:28.760
That's not true!

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:33.670
She'd practically become a maid for me if I'd let her, so I thought I'd at least let her make breakfast!

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:34.820
For real.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.820
Kirino hasn't changed either.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.690
Don't get the wrong idea...

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:42.720
I'm not. Anyway, go clean the toilet or something.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:44.070
Right now!?

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:48.130
We'll be living together again, so try to keep things clean.

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:49.550
All right, all right.

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:53.090
Once you finish cleaning, I want you to install what's in that bag.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:56.800
What's this?

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.890
Slippers, a seat cover and a mat.

00:11:02.890 --> 00:11:05.310
And a toilet paper holder.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.400
Ooh, fancy.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:09.940
Hurry up and get to work!

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:11.020
R-Right away!

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.200
Oh boy...

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:16.190
"We'll be living together again," huh?

00:11:21.750 --> 00:11:24.700
Hey, how long are you going to keep sleeping?

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.360
Wake up already! We're running late!

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:31.960
Be a bit more gentle...

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:36.010
Stop being such a wuss!

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:38.990
Are you awake now?

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:41.930
What a great way to wake up...

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:42.800
<i>Number One</i>

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.440
D-Don't look!

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.100
Don't make a big deal out of it.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:06.870
Geez. Why do I have to have people peeking up my skirt early in the morning...

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:08.390
So it's okay to peek in the evening?

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:09.270
Moron.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.610
Haruhiko-kun, are you okay?

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:15.820
Not at all. At least you wouldn't mind me looking at your panties, would you?

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:18.350
N-No... I guess...

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:20.650
No need to play along with that fool.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:22.970
Anyway, sorry for having you make breakfast.

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:24.280
That's all right.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:27.550
At any rate, it's really luxurious today...

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:29.700
It's because Riko has returned.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.560
So it's a sort of celebration.

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:39.570
It'd be great if we ended up in the same class.

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.620
You're my little sister, so that's impossible.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.520
But we're the same age.

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:45.530
Oh, right.

00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.210
Did you say that on purpose?

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:48.270
Nope.

00:12:48.270 --> 00:12:54.400
But thinking of you as my little sister is the only way for me to accept you straddling me to wake me up in the morning.

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:55.960
T-That's not true!

00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.370
Man, don't make it so easy for people to misunderstand!

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.420
T-That girl...

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:06.550
What's that?

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:12.660
Did you know there is a magician girl in this town?

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.350
They say she makes all kinds of wishes come true.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:17.170
Really?

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:21.470
Like kicking people off her broom from high in the sky...

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.550
Let me introduce you to our new transfer student.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:30.030
I'm Fukamine Riko. Nice to meet you all!

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.330
Wait, what?

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:42.050
If I may add a footnote, Fukamine-san is Amami-kun's non-related little sister.

00:13:44.080 --> 00:13:47.830
A young man and woman not related by blood living under the same roof...

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:51.040
Err...

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:54.630
Well, anything goes while you're still young.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.290
Err, we haven't been doing a thing...

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:01.470
However if you had been too young, God might have forgiven you for it but I would not have!

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.250
Time to take a round of the school.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:11.560
Sorry to have you show me around.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:13.580
Well, I'm fine with that, but...

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.820
...what's up with that?

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:22.750
The fate of the transfer student.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:28.290
Adding Amami into that group would probably initiate some chemical reaction...

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:29.300
Please stop.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.560
It's so exciting!

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.250
- Ah, Haruhiko-kun!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:34.360
Why are you carrying a broom?

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:37.030
We're cleaning while inspecting the school grounds.

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:39.260
That is quite practical.

00:14:39.260 --> 00:14:41.810
This is my friend Fujimiya Chisa.

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:45.680
This is Fukamine Riko. Haruhiko-kun's little sister.

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:47.740
Nice to meet you.

00:14:48.040 --> 00:14:50.730
I'm Fujimiya Chisa. Nice to meet you too.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:55.480
Err...

00:14:55.850 --> 00:15:00.030
Somehow, you and that broom seem to make an awfully good match...

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:01.080
I wonder why...

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:04.310
I-It's just your imagination!

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:05.370
That's what I figured!

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:14.310
It might be a good idea to wrap up this meeting and relocate.

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.100
I have a feeling a chemical reaction is about to occur.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.430
Let's move!

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:23.710
Wait!

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.820
We weren't able to witness a Big Bang...

00:15:30.510 --> 00:15:33.040
Geez, Onii-chan!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:42.580
Huh? Who's that?

00:15:43.410 --> 00:15:45.140
She got into that fight the other day...

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.670
That's Hokazono Rinka.

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:51.320
She's a master of the Ousou sword style, and acted as a teacher at the kendo club in junior high.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:53.230
I see, it figures.

00:15:53.230 --> 00:15:54.300
When did you get here!?

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:01.120
She's quite a looker.

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.760
How long are you going to stare?

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.670
I can see right through your every move!

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:16.090
What the...

00:16:18.280 --> 00:16:19.680
What's that?

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:21.630
One of Rinka's training contraptions.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:23.290
It is truly marvelous.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:26.790
That kind of circular movement is mechanically beautiful.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:35.050
You got what was coming for you.

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.580
Ouch...

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:41.290
Good thing Yukarin happened to pass by.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:44.140
The school is full of danger, is it not?

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:47.140
Excuse me.

00:16:49.730 --> 00:16:51.400
I am truly sorry.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:53.270
It's fine, it's fine!

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:55.700
So, err, who are you?

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:59.390
Kamishiro Yukari. Please call me "Yukarin."

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:05.080
Yukarin is working as a maid at my house.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:07.370
You seem wise for your age.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.130
Not at all!

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:15.660
Riko-san and Kirino-san, good luck with your new daily life.

00:17:15.660 --> 00:17:17.340
Thank you.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.010
You be careful as well, Amami-san.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.710
Let us go, ladies.

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:31.670
It seems Amami has some business to attend to.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:40.200
Ow...

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.950
Onii-chan, are you okay?

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.540
Damn...

00:17:43.930 --> 00:17:46.160
A man's jealousy is terrifying...

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:48.920
Amami, it's noisy on the school grounds.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:51.900
We won't allow for you to cause trouble.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:53.860
We won't!

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.900
We will not.

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:58.190
It's not my fault!

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.030
Is that so?

00:18:00.030 --> 00:18:01.230
Oh really?

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:02.950
I wonder about that.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.070
Every single one...

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.010
It's your first day here, but you must be sick of this school already.

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.380
No, it seems like great fun!

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:17.200
After all, I'm able to attend school together with you!

00:18:18.340 --> 00:18:20.950
Don't say that in front of those guys.

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:26.320
Riko-chan, welcome back!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:30.330
You really like doing that, don't you Tama-nee?

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.200
Oh, do you want me to do it to you too?

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:34.530
No thanks.

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:37.030
Why not!?

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.130
Huh? Riko-chan, do you have a cold?

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:41.640
What're you talking about?

00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:43.780
Well, shall we begin?

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:45.720
Everyone, raise your glasses.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:53.520
Haruhiko, will you give a toast?

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:54.780
Me?

00:18:55.100 --> 00:18:57.860
I'm no good at speeches.

00:18:57.860 --> 00:18:59.680
You have an awful way with words.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:05.400
I nearly turned a wedding ceremony into pandemonium that way once!

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:07.590
That's not really something to laugh about.

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:09.460
Come on, Haruhiko-chan!

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:12.580
Well then... cheers!

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.940
That's it!?

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:16.730
He's a shy guy after all!

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:20.050
So, that was the toast?

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:21.970
I'm really glad.

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.580
At that time, I was truly sad.

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:30.470
Anyway...

00:19:31.220 --> 00:19:34.580
I'm really glad you came back.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:36.460
Onii-chan...

00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:47.040
Come on! The food I made is growing cold, so hurry up...

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.450
Okay. Cheers!

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.290
Cheers!

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:54.170
Tama-nee, you're killing him!

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:55.630
Let him go!

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.100
Are you okay?

00:19:57.100 --> 00:19:58.550
I died two or three times...

00:19:58.550 --> 00:20:00.460
Hey, Haruhiko! You drink too!

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:02.170
I'm a minor!

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:08.670
I'm really happy Riko-chan came back!

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:13.070
I hope they'll get along as well as they used to!

00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:12.860
- What's up?

00:20:13.070 --> 00:20:16.080
The origin of that rainbow is still unknown, right?

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:17.110
Yeah.

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.390
But you're happy, right?

00:20:19.390 --> 00:20:20.250
About what?

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:22.370
You loved rainbows, didn't you?

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:24.900
You're mistaken.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:26.870
Really?

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.040
My mother was the one who loved rainbows.

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.540
Didn't Dad talk about that often?

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:34.740
I see...

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:38.340
Kirino-chan is saying she's going home now!

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:40.760
She wants you to walk her back to her house.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:44.850
Walk you back? You live next door.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:46.910
Can we take a little walk?

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:54.880
You know, I think that things will have to change from how they used to be.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.400
How they used to be?

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:01.510
Like me coming over in the morning to wake you and making you breakfast...

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:02.340
Why?

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:05.580
Well, Riko-chan came back.

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.540
Is it too tough to make breakfast for two?

00:21:07.540 --> 00:21:09.200
That's not what I mean...

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:16.300
I'm sure Riko-chan wants to do those things herself as well.

00:21:19.830 --> 00:21:21.900
Meaning you're stepping down for Riko?

00:21:22.410 --> 00:21:24.370
That's... right.

00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:30.750
I understand.

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.940
That's all I wanted to say.

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:34.730
Bye!

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:35.640
Kirino!

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:40.080
Instead, I'll come and pick you up when it's time for school.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:43.920
I at least want the three of us to walk to school together.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:45.650
That's true.

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:50.290
Sorry...

00:21:50.620 --> 00:21:53.420
What are you apologizing for? Stupid.

